<DocsBase title="Overview" section="Getting started">
  <h1>EGAC Platform</h1>

  <p>
    This is the internal developer and operator wiki for the East Grinstead Athletics Club platform.
    It covers how the system is built, why key decisions were made, and how to run, deploy, and
    extend it.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    <p>
      <strong>Internal only.</strong> This documentation is not publicly indexed. Do not share direct
      links outside the club.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>What the platform does</h2>

  <p>
    The platform manages the full lifecycle of an athlete enquiry — from a parent filling in the
    website form through to a confirmed taster session or an Academy waitlist place.
  </p>

  <p>There are two journeys, determined automatically by the athlete's age group:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Taster booking</strong> — the enquirer receives a tokenised invite link by email, picks
      a session date from the next available Tuesdays, and gets a confirmation with a Google Calendar
      link.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Academy waitlist</strong> — the enquirer is placed on the waitlist for the current Academy
      season. When a place becomes available, an invite is sent and they respond via a dedicated page.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Age group assignment follows UK Athletics rules: an athlete's group is determined by their age
    on <strong>31 August</strong> at the end of the relevant athletics season, not by their birthday or
    the session date.
  </p>

  <h2>Technology stack</h2>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technology</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Framework</td><td>Astro 4 (SSR mode)</td><td>Pages, admin UI, API routing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Runtime</td><td>Cloudflare Workers</td><td>Edge compute, cron triggers</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Hosting</td><td>Cloudflare Pages</td><td>Static + SSR deployment</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Database</td><td>Cloudflare D1 (SQLite)</td><td>All persistent data</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cache / config</td><td>Cloudflare KV</td><td>System config with 5-min TTL</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Email</td><td>Resend REST API</td><td>Transactional email, no SDK</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Language</td><td>TypeScript 5 (strict)</td><td>End-to-end type safety</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Styling</td><td>Tailwind CSS 3</td><td>Admin UI and public pages</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Testing</td><td>Vitest + Miniflare</td><td>Unit tests against local Workers</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Deploy tooling</td><td>Wrangler 3</td><td>D1 migrations, secrets, deploys</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Source layout</h2>

  <pre><code>src/
  api/            API route handlers (enquiry, booking, academy, admin/*, cron/*)
  lib/
    business/     Pure business logic — age rules, booking validation, templates
    repositories/ D1 data access — one file per entity
    email/        Email client (Resend) and per-email-type sender functions
    auth/         Admin token checking (cookie + Bearer header)
    config.ts     KV-backed system config with defaults
    db/           D1 client, ID generation, schema types
  pages/
    admin/        Server-rendered admin portal pages
    docs/         This documentation
    book/         Public booking confirmation page (tokenised)
    academy/      Academy waitlist response page (tokenised)
  layouts/        AdminBase, DocsBase, Layout, Base
  workers/        coach-app.js (separate Worker)
db/
  migrations/     Numbered SQL migration files
  seed.sql        Local development seed data
tests/
  unit/           Vitest unit tests</code></pre>

  <h2>Key flows</h2>

  <h3>Enquiry → taster invite</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Parent submits the public enquiry form (<code>POST /api/enquiry</code>).</li>
    <li>
      Age group is resolved from D1 using the athlete's date of birth and the UK Athletics 31 August
      rule.
    </li>
    <li>
      If the age group's <code>booking_type</code> is <code>taster</code>, a tokenised invite record
      is created and a booking invite email is sent via Resend.
    </li>
    <li>
      Parent clicks the link, lands on <code>/book/[token]</code>, picks a date, and
      <code>POST /api/booking</code> confirms the session.
    </li>
    <li>A confirmation email with venue details and a Google Calendar link is sent.</li>
    <li>Seven days before the session a reminder email is sent by the Tuesday-evening cron job.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Enquiry → Academy waitlist</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Same enquiry form submission.</li>
    <li>Age group resolves to <code>booking_type: waitlist</code>.</li>
    <li>Enquiry is added to <code>academy_waitlist</code> for the current open season.</li>
    <li>An Academy waitlist confirmation email is sent.</li>
    <li>
      When a place opens, an Academy invite is sent. Parent responds via
      <code>/academy/respond/[token]</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      On the 1st of each month the academy-rollover cron carries returning athletes forward to the
      next season.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Database tables</h2>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Table</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td><code>enquiries</code></td><td
          >Central record for every inbound enquiry. Holds the event log (JSON array) tracking every
          status change.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>invites</code></td><td
          >Tokenised booking invites for taster sessions. One per enquiry, status: pending → sent →
          accepted → expired.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>bookings</code></td><td
          >Confirmed taster sessions. Status: confirmed → attended / no_show / cancelled.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>age_groups</code></td><td
          >Fully configurable in D1 — no age group codes are hardcoded in application logic. Drives
          routing and session scheduling.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>academy_seasons</code></td><td
          >Each Academy intake season with capacity, dates, and status (upcoming / open / closed /
          archived).</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>academy_waitlist</code></td><td
          >One entry per enquiry per season. Tracks position, invite status, and response.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>email_templates</code></td><td
          >Editable email templates stored in D1. Rendered at send time with simple template
          variable substitution.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>membership_otps</code></td><td>One-time tokens for the membership form flow.</td
        ></tr
      >
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cron schedule</h2>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Schedule</th><th>Job</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td><code>0 9 * * *</code></td><td>expire-invites</td><td
          >Marks stale pending invites as expired.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>0 18 * * 2</code></td><td>send-reminders</td><td
          >Sends reminder emails for sessions 7 days ahead (Tuesday evenings).</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>*/30 * * * *</code></td><td>retry-invites</td><td
          >Retries invite sends that previously failed due to email errors.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>0 9 1 * *</code></td><td>academy-rollover</td><td
          >Carries returning Academy athletes forward to the next season on the 1st of each month.</td
        ></tr
      >
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Cron jobs are also callable via HTTP (<code>POST /api/cron/*</code>) using
    <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;CRON_SECRET&gt;</code> — useful for manual runs and testing.
  </p>

  <h2>Authentication</h2>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Route group</th><th>Mechanism</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td
          >Public routes (<code>/api/enquiry</code>, <code>/api/booking</code>, <code
            >/api/academy/respond</code
          >)</td
        ><td>No authentication. Rate limiting is handled at the Cloudflare edge.</td></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td>Admin portal pages (<code>/admin/*</code>)</td><td
          >HttpOnly cookie <code>egac_admin_token</code>, set on login. Checked server-side in every
          page's frontmatter.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td>Admin API (<code>/api/admin/*</code>)</td><td
          ><code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;ADMIN_TOKEN&gt;</code> or <code>x-admin-token</code> header.</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td>Cron routes (<code>/api/cron/*</code>)</td><td
          ><code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;CRON_SECRET&gt;</code> — a separate secret from <code
            >ADMIN_TOKEN</code
          >.</td
        ></tr
      >
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    In local development only, the token <code>dev</code> is accepted for both admin and cron routes.
    This shorthand is rejected if <code>APP_ENV</code> is anything other than
    <code>development</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Environment variables</h2>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>How set</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr
        ><td><code>APP_ENV</code></td><td><code>wrangler.toml [vars]</code></td><td
          ><code>production</code> | <code>staging</code> | <code>development</code></td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>EMAIL_FROM</code></td><td><code>wrangler.toml [vars]</code></td><td
          >Sender address for all outbound email</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>RESEND_API_KEY</code></td><td><code>wrangler secret put</code></td><td
          >Resend authentication</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>ADMIN_TOKEN</code></td><td><code>wrangler secret put</code></td><td
          >Admin portal and API authentication</td
        ></tr
      >
      <tr
        ><td><code>CRON_SECRET</code></td><td><code>wrangler secret put</code></td><td
          >Cron job HTTP authentication</td
        ></tr
      >
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Running locally</h2>

  <pre><code># Install dependencies
npm install

# Apply migrations and seed data to the local D1 database
npm run migrate:local
npm run migrate:seed

# Start the dev server (Wrangler + Astro)
npm run dev</code></pre>

  <p>
    The admin portal is available at <code>http://localhost:4321/admin</code>. Use the token
    <code>dev</code> to log in during local development.
  </p>

  <h2>Running tests</h2>

  <pre><code># Run all tests once
npm test

# Watch mode
npm run test:watch

# Coverage report
npm run test:coverage

# Type check
npm run type-check

# Lint (zero warnings enforced)
npm run lint</code></pre>

  <h2>Deploying</h2>

  <pre><code># Deploy to production (Cloudflare Pages)
npx wrangler pages deploy dist

# Apply a new migration to production D1
wrangler d1 execute egac --file=db/migrations/0002_membership_forms.sql

# Set or rotate a secret
wrangler secret put ADMIN_TOKEN</code></pre>

  <hr />

  <p>
    Use the sidebar to navigate to more detailed pages on specific topics. If a page shows "coming
    soon", the content hasn't been written yet — add it to <code>src/pages/docs/</code>
    using the <code>DocsBase</code> layout.
  </p>
